"<div class=\"sphx-glr-thumbcontainer\" tooltip=\"This projection was "
"developed by Johann Heinrich Lambert in 1772 and is typically used for "
"mapping large regions like continents and hemispheres. It is an azimuthal, "
"equal-area projection, but is not perspective. Distortion is zero at the "
"center of the projection, and increases radially away from this point.\">"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../examples/tutorials/basics/text.py:1388
msgid ":doc:`/projections/azim/azim_lambert`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../examples/tutorials/basics/text.py:1390
